      </nav>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ol class="refs">
        <li id="r1">Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, Consumer Price Index for
          June 2026, press release, 13 July 2026. Series 2024=100, provisional.</li>
        <li id="r2">MoSPI CPI (2024 series), education services division, NCT of Delhi, combined,
          year-on-year. Retrieved from the eSankhyiki CPI service.</li>
        <li id="r3"><a href="https://www.mospi.gov.in/uploads/documents/documents/1770891066052-Annexure_V.pdf">MoSPI,
          FAQs on the CPI 2024 series (Annexure V)</a> &mdash; basket, weights, collection network,
          alternative price sources, formulas, and the linking factors between the two series
          (all-India combined 0.5267, rural 0.5222, urban 0.5320; each reproduced here as the ratio
          of the two series&rsquo; geometric means over the twelve overlap months of 2025).
          Elementary indices are compiled per state and sector; every higher index is a
          weighted fold within its sector, and rural and urban are blended at every published
          level &mdash; &ldquo;combined&rdquo; throughout this read is that blend. Basket weights for both vintages are compared
          on the 2024 (COICOP 2018) classification structure throughout, the like-for-like basis
          MoSPI itself recommends (FAQ 40); cross-structure comparisons give different
          figures.</li>
        <li id="r4"><a href="https://www.outlookindia.com/national/delhi-private-schools-must-justify-fee-hikes-as-govt-releases-18-parameters">&ldquo;Delhi private schools must justify fee hikes as govt releases 18 parameters&rdquo;</a>, Outlook India, 2026.</li>
        <li id="r5"><a href="https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/delhi/delhi-private-schools-must-set-up-fee-regulation-committees-for-2026-27-doe-issues-fresh-guidelines/">&ldquo;Delhi private schools must set up fee regulation committees for 2026-27&rdquo;</a>, The Tribune, 2026.</li>
        {/* Renumbered contiguously in the Aug 2026 pass (old r8/r15/r16/r17 → r6-r9); the
            in-text superscripts now match the <ol>'s rendered numbers. Cut along the way,
            all recoverable from git history: the drift figure + UK RPI sources (return with the
            planned averaging collapsible), the five-machines press sources (r9-r13), and
            the Onmanorama state-ranking piece (r14, left with the rank-turnover cut). */}
        <li id="r6">MoSPI / National Sample Survey, Household Consumption Expenditure Survey
          2023&ndash;24 &mdash; the source of the 2024-series weights.</li>
        <li id="r7"><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/rbi-mpc-december-2025-rate-cut-announcement-sanjay-malhotra-cpi-inflation-125120500161_1.html">&ldquo;RBI
          MPC cuts repo rate by 25 bps to 5.25%&rdquo;</a>, Business Standard, 5 December 2025.
          The staircase itself is hand-keyed from RBI Monetary Policy Committee announcements,
          2014 through the June 2026 hold.</li>
        <li id="r8">MoSPI, CPI (2024 series) item indices and the Annexure 5.3 weighing
          diagram, All India Combined, {month} &mdash; the item contributions, and the same
